00:12:11,500 --> 00:12:13,500
you know, just as a rule of thumb,

261
00:12:13,500 --> 00:12:15,500
people will begin to get on board,

262
00:12:15,500 --> 00:12:17,500
get them to write those things down

263
00:12:17,500 --> 00:12:18,500
and then, in my opinion,

264
00:12:18,500 --> 00:12:20,500
you really want the senior patrol leader

265
00:12:20,500 --> 00:12:21,500
making those announcements.

266
00:12:21,500 --> 00:12:23,500
So around here we call

267
00:12:23,500 --> 00:12:24,500
becoming a Scout Master

268
00:12:24,500 --> 00:12:26,500
jumping into the volcano.

269
00:12:26,500 --> 00:12:28,500
It's a little overwhelming at first,

270
00:12:28,500 --> 00:12:30,500
but don't worry. as you get some experience

271
00:12:30,500 --> 00:12:32,500
and observe what is going on with your Scouts,

272
00:12:32,500 --> 00:12:34,500
you'll gain confidence in your judgment

273
00:12:34,500 --> 00:12:36,500
of what's important and what isn't.

274
00:12:36,500 --> 00:12:38,500
Take all the time you can

275
00:12:38,500 --> 00:12:40,500
to study and learn about your role

276
00:12:40,500 --> 00:12:42,500
and put that knowledge to work.

277
00:12:42,500 --> 00:12:44,500
If your heart's in the right place,

278
00:12:44,500 --> 00:12:46,500
it's not likely you're going to do any harm.

279
00:12:46,500 --> 00:12:48,500
What you'll do is a lot of good.

280
00:12:48,500 --> 00:12:50,500
Vin Cervantes is in Massachusetts

281
00:12:50,500 --> 00:12:52,500
and he asked:

282
00:12:52,500 --> 00:12:54,500
have you ever written or spoken about

283
00:12:54,500 --> 00:12:56,500
calling Scouts Scouts

284
00:12:56,500 --> 00:12:58,500
rather than boys or kids?

285
00:12:58,500 --> 00:13:00,500
Well, hey, Vin,

286
00:13:00,500 --> 00:13:02,500
I can't recall ever really going into much depth

287
00:13:02,500 --> 00:13:03,500
on the question.

288
00:13:03,500 --> 00:13:05,500
I know that I sent this out

289
00:13:05,500 --> 00:13:07,500
as a tweet a while back.

290
00:13:07,500 --> 00:13:09,500
If you want your Scouts to act like Scouts,

291
00:13:09,500 --> 00:13:11,500
call them Scouts.

292
00:13:11,500 --> 00:13:13,500
If you call them kids,

293
00:13:13,500 --> 00:13:14,500
they'll act like kids.

294
00:13:14,500 --> 00:13:15,500
I think it is true.

295
00:13:15,500 --> 00:13:17,500
I think you tend to get what you expect.

296
00:13:17,500 --> 00:13:19,500
and if you want your Scouts

297
00:13:19,500 --> 00:13:20,500
to act like Scouts

298
00:13:20,500 --> 00:13:21,500
and to be Scouts.

299
00:13:21,500 --> 00:13:23,500
I would avoid calling them anything else.

300
00:13:23,500 --> 00:13:25,500
Gary Gomez works with

301
00:13:25,500 --> 00:13:27,500
Boy Scout Troop in San Diego, California,

302
00:13:27,500 --> 00:13:29,500
and he wrote in to ask:

303
00:13:29,500 --> 00:13:31,500
I was curious as to what you think about

304
00:13:31,500 --> 00:13:33,500
having prerequisites

305
00:13:33,500 --> 00:13:35,500
for positions of responsibility, such as age

306
00:13:35,500 --> 00:13:37,500
or number of years in Scouting, etc.

307
00:13:37,500 --> 00:13:39,500
Should a Scout be required to be a patroller

308
00:13:39,500 --> 00:13:41,500
before being allowed to run

309
00:13:41,500 --> 00:13:43,500
for senior patroller?

310
00:13:43,500 --> 00:13:45,500
I can see both pros and cons,

311
00:13:45,500 --> 00:13:47,500
wondering what your experience is.

312
00:13:47,500 --> 00:13:49,500
Well, Gary, I think

313
00:13:49,500 --> 00:13:50,500
either way works

314
00:13:50,500 --> 00:13:52,500
In my troop. in my troop,

315
00:13:52,500 --> 00:13:54,500
we don't have prerequisites for this

316
00:13:54,500 --> 00:13:56,500
and things seem to go fine.

317
00:13:56,500 --> 00:13:58,500
Scouts make very good decisions.

318
00:13:58,500 --> 00:14:00,500
They have prerequisites in their own minds

319
00:14:00,500 --> 00:14:02,500
when they're voting for a patroller

320
00:14:02,500 --> 00:14:03,500
or senior patroller.

321
00:14:03,500 --> 00:14:05,500
Scouts ought to be reminded

322
00:14:05,500 --> 00:14:06,500
about the seriousness of it

323
00:14:06,500 --> 00:14:08,500
and when they take it seriously,

324
00:14:08,500 --> 00:14:10,500
they'll make very good choices.

325
00:14:10,500 --> 00:14:12,500
What I've found is, if we create

326
00:14:12,500 --> 00:14:14,500
these kind of rules,

327
00:14:14,500 --> 00:14:16,500
we can set up a whole list of prerequisites

328
00:14:16,500 --> 00:14:18,500
that Scouts need to have

329
00:14:18,500 --> 00:14:20,500
before they can run for patroller

330
00:14:20,500 --> 00:14:22,500
or senior patroller.

331
00:14:22,500 --> 00:14:24,500
as soon as the ink dries on those rules,

332
00:14:24,500 --> 00:14:26,500
we're faced with a situation

333
00:14:26,500 --> 00:14:28,500
that's an exception to the rule.

334
00:14:28,500 --> 00:14:30,500
so I'm not saying that you can't have them.

335
00:14:30,500 --> 00:14:32,500
what I'm saying is,

336
00:14:32,500 --> 00:14:34,500
in my experience, you don't need them.

337
00:14:34,500 --> 00:14:36,500
I am withholding the name

338
00:14:36,500 --> 00:14:38,500
of the person who sent me this next email

339
00:14:38,500 --> 00:14:40,500
for what will become obvious reasons.

340
00:14:40,500 --> 00:14:42,500
I've been following your blog

341
00:14:42,500 --> 00:14:44,500
and your opinion on all things scouting.

342
00:14:44,500 --> 00:14:46,500
My son is 15,

343
00:14:46,500 --> 00:14:48,500
a high school sophomore,

344
00:14:48,500 --> 00:14:50,500
and has almost completed everything he needs

345
00:14:50,500 --> 00:14:52,500
to become an Eagle Scout.

346
00:14:52,500 --> 00:14:54,500
He's been an active youth leader and scout.

347
00:14:54,500 --> 00:14:56,500
he's earned his religious emblems.

348
00:14:56,500 --> 00:14:58,500
he's active in the OA.

349
00:14:58,500 --> 00:15:00,500
he's been to two national jamborees.

350
00:15:00,500 --> 00:15:02,500
he's been to Fillmont, Northern Tier,

351
00:15:02,500 --> 00:15:04,500
and he's headed to Seabase

352
00:15:04,500 --> 00:15:06,500
over Spring Break this year

353
00:15:06,500 --> 00:15:08,500
and then back to Northern Tier this summer

354
00:15:08,500 --> 00:15:10,500
with the OA program.

355
00:15:10,500 --> 00:15:12,500
He's a former medal.

356
00:15:12,500 --> 00:15:14,500
he's also in the international

357
00:15:14,500 --> 00:15:16,500
baccalaureate program at school.

358
00:15:16,500 --> 00:15:18,500
he loves scouting

359
00:15:18,500 --> 00:15:20,500
and all it has to offer,

360
00:15:20,500 --> 00:15:22,500
especially those high adventure opportunities.

361
00:15:22,500 --> 00:15:24,500
our troop has recently formed

362
00:15:24,500 --> 00:15:26,500
what they call a venture patrol,

363
00:15:26,500 --> 00:15:28,500
but my son is a little put off

364
00:15:28,500 --> 00:15:30,500
by the fact that he's been presented

365
00:15:30,500 --> 00:15:32,500
with a venture patrol contract

366
00:15:32,500 --> 00:15:34,500
and the contract has a number of stipulations.

367
00:15:34,500 --> 00:15:36,500
one is that scouts have to be 14

368
00:15:36,500 --> 00:15:38,500
and older, they have to be

369
00:15:38,500 --> 00:15:40,500
15 and higher and they have to have

370
00:15:40,500 --> 00:15:42,500
over 70% attendance

371
00:15:42,500 --> 00:15:44,500
in the past six months.

372
00:15:44,500 --> 00:15:46,500
they also must attend and participate

373
00:15:46,500 --> 00:15:48,500
in 75% of the meetings, troop outing

374
00:15:48,500 --> 00:15:50,500
and service projects,

375
00:15:50,500 --> 00:15:52,500
and it says in the contract if their attendance is too low

376
00:15:52,500 --> 00:15:54,500
or there are three-

377
00:15:54,500 --> 00:15:56,500
quote- unexcused absences-

378
00:15:56,500 --> 00:15:58,500
unquote- the scout master has a discretion

379
00:15:58,500 --> 00:16:00,500
to take punitive action

380
00:16:00,500 --> 00:16:02,500
towards them. it says they have to wear

381
00:16:02,500 --> 00:16:04,500
the uniform correctly and set an example

382
00:16:04,500 --> 00:16:06,500
in behavior. and set an example.

383
00:16:06,500 --> 00:16:08,500
it says on camp out the venture patrol

384
00:16:08,500 --> 00:16:10,500
won't be able to set up their camp

385
00:16:10,500 --> 00:16:12,500
until the entire troop is set up.

386
00:16:12,500 --> 00:16:14,500
that the venture patrol runs

387
00:16:14,500 --> 00:16:16,500
the Sunday night campfire on every camp out.

388
00:16:16,500 --> 00:16:18,500
that the venture patrol has got to be

389
00:16:18,500 --> 00:16:20,500
the last ones to bed

390
00:16:20,500 --> 00:16:22,500
and the first ones up in the morning.

391
00:16:22,500 --> 00:16:24,500
and finally, it says that any

392
00:16:24,500 --> 00:16:26,500
high adventure activities that the venture patrol

393
00:16:26,500 --> 00:16:28,500
plans can't compete with the

394
00:16:28,500 --> 00:16:30,500
regularly scheduled troop activities.

395
00:16:30,500 --> 00:16:32,500
I looked at this contract with my son

396
00:16:32,500 --> 00:16:34,500
and there are a lot of things in it

397
00:16:34,500 --> 00:16:36,500
that don't sit well with either of us.

398
00:16:36,500 --> 00:16:38,500
I assume it was created without

399
00:16:38,500 --> 00:16:40,500
any youth input.

400
00:16:40,500 --> 00:16:42,500
it seems more exclusionary,

401
00:16:42,500 --> 00:16:44,500
designed to keep scouts out rather than

402
00:16:44,500 --> 00:16:46,500
keep them engaged in the scouting program.

403
00:16:46,500 --> 00:16:48,500
it all seems kind of heavy handed,

404
00:16:48,500 --> 00:16:50,500
with punitive undertones on the adult side.

405
00:16:50,500 --> 00:16:52,500
I would very much appreciate

406
00:16:52,500 --> 00:16:54,500
any insight you might have about this.

407
00:16:54,500 --> 00:16:56,500
wow,

408
00:16:56,500 --> 00:16:58,500
well, every once in a while

409
00:16:58,500 --> 00:17:00,500
it's just amazing how many different

410
00:17:00,500 --> 00:17:02,500
ways we can find

411
00:17:02,500 --> 00:17:04,500
to squelch the enthusiasm of scouts.

412
00:17:04,500 --> 00:17:06,500
I'm going to be a little

413
00:17:06,500 --> 00:17:08,500
snarky here, but I'll bet that

414
00:17:08,500 --> 00:17:10,500
the adults that came up with this

415
00:17:10,500 --> 00:17:12,500
contract are all men,

416
00:17:12,500 --> 00:17:14,500
because women are usually quite a bit smarter

417
00:17:14,500 --> 00:17:16,500
when it comes to this type of thing.

418
00:17:16,500 --> 00:17:18,500
now, from what I read in this

419
00:17:18,500 --> 00:17:20,500
email, here's a scout who would

420
00:17:20,500 --> 00:17:22,500
do all the things on this contract

421
00:17:22,500 --> 00:17:24,500
voluntarily,

422
00:17:24,500 --> 00:17:26,500
but he's turned off by the idea of

423
00:17:26,500 --> 00:17:28,500
somebody forcing him to do them

424
00:17:28,500 --> 00:17:30,500
and who wouldn't be. frankly,

425
00:17:30,500 --> 00:17:32,500
perhaps I can offer an explanation

426
00:17:32,500 --> 00:17:34,500
of why this feels

427
00:17:34,500 --> 00:17:36,500
and why this is so wrong.

428
00:17:36,500 --> 00:17:38,500
it's

429
00:17:38,500 --> 00:17:40,500
the first point of the scout law

430
00:17:40,500 --> 00:17:42,500
and that is what

431
00:17:42,500 --> 00:17:44,500
a scout is trustworthy.

432
00:17:44,500 --> 00:17:46,500
the explicit message of

433
00:17:46,500 --> 00:17:48,500
requiring a contract

434
00:17:48,500 --> 00:17:50,500
from a scout is that

435
00:17:50,500 --> 00:17:52,500
without a way to force you to do things,

436
00:17:52,500 --> 00:17:54,500
we can't trust you

437
00:17:54,500 --> 00:17:56,500
or respect your word.

438
00:17:56,500 --> 00:17:58,500
now, in a business context,

439
00:17:58,500 --> 00:18:00,500
or good, necessary tools

440
00:18:00,500 --> 00:18:02,500
in scouting, I find them

441
00:18:02,500 --> 00:18:04,500
downright offensive as well as

442
00:18:04,500 --> 00:18:06,500
inimical to the entire foundation

443
00:18:06,500 --> 00:18:08,500
of our work.

444
00:18:08,500 --> 00:18:10,500
a scout is

445
00:18:10,500 --> 00:18:12,500
trustworthy. you can't

446
00:18:12,500 --> 00:18:14,500
reduce trustworthiness to a piece of paper

447
00:18:14,500 --> 00:18:16,500
and, as any parent knows,

448
00:18:16,500 --> 00:18:18,500
you're not going to force

449
00:18:18,500 --> 00:18:20,500
a 15 year old to do anything

450
00:18:20,500 --> 00:18:22,500
because he's put his name

