00:20:42,500 --> 00:20:44,500
6 to over 100 scouts.

522
00:20:44,500 --> 00:20:46,500
what would be the largest a troop

523
00:20:46,500 --> 00:20:48,500
would be? instill, deliver the promise of scouting

524
00:20:48,500 --> 00:20:50,500
and ensure that every scout gets

525
00:20:50,500 --> 00:20:52,500
the best possible experience.

526
00:20:52,500 --> 00:20:54,500
our troop has experienced tremendous

527
00:20:54,500 --> 00:20:56,500
growth. if we look into the future-

528
00:20:56,500 --> 00:20:58,500
maybe 2 or 3 years- we could easily

529
00:20:58,500 --> 00:21:00,500
well be north of 100 scouts.

530
00:21:00,500 --> 00:21:02,500
myself and other adults are asking

531
00:21:02,500 --> 00:21:04,500
ourselves: how do we know

532
00:21:04,500 --> 00:21:06,500
if we're getting too big? I know

533
00:21:06,500 --> 00:21:08,500
there's no hard or fast rules or a

