00:21:22,500 --> 00:21:24,500
does have a scale. for instance,

542
00:21:24,500 --> 00:21:26,500
we know patrols work best

543
00:21:26,500 --> 00:21:28,500
when they number between 6 and 10,

544
00:21:28,500 --> 00:21:30,500
but the size of troops is really an

545
00:21:30,500 --> 00:21:32,500
open question. what's really

546
00:21:32,500 --> 00:21:34,500
important is patrols. the patrol

547
00:21:34,500 --> 00:21:36,500
is the scale of scouting.

548
00:21:36,500 --> 00:21:38,500
Baden Powell frequently emphasize

549
00:21:38,500 --> 00:21:40,500
that a scout should never feel

550
00:21:40,500 --> 00:21:42,500
as though he's just member of

551
00:21:42,500 --> 00:21:44,500
a great, vast herd of scouts.

552
00:21:44,500 --> 00:21:46,500
any scout should know

553
00:21:46,500 --> 00:21:48,500
and work with his patrol

554
00:21:48,500 --> 00:21:50,500
and feel that he's known and appreciated

555
00:21:50,500 --> 00:21:52,500
in his patrol and in his troop.

556
00:21:52,500 --> 00:21:54,500
youth leaders also need to be able to

557
00:21:54,500 --> 00:21:56,500
work and plan at a scale

558
00:21:56,500 --> 00:21:58,500
that's realizable for them.

559
00:21:58,500 --> 00:22:00,500
some big troops pull this off

560
00:22:00,500 --> 00:22:02,500
