656
00:25:12,500 --> 00:25:14,500
or appreciated. scouts get this.

657
00:25:14,500 --> 00:25:16,500
they know that they promise to be

658
00:25:16,500 --> 00:25:18,500
friendly, helpful and kind.

659
00:25:18,500 --> 00:25:20,500
that's something we usually think

660
00:25:20,500 --> 00:25:22,500
about as individuals, but

661
00:25:22,500 --> 00:25:24,500
can they tell you

662
00:25:24,500 --> 00:25:26,500
how they do that as a group

663
00:25:26,500 --> 00:25:28,500
of scouts? can they be

664
00:25:28,500 --> 00:25:30,500
helpful, friendly and kind?

665
00:25:30,500 --> 00:25:32,500
as a patrol leaders counsel, you may

666
00:25:32,500 --> 00:25:34,500
have a story about how you overcame

667
00:25:34,500 --> 00:25:36,500
first impressions in the frustration

668
00:25:36,500 --> 00:25:38,500
of dealing with somebody who had

669
00:25:38,500 --> 00:25:40,500
limitations over which they had no control.

670
00:25:40,500 --> 00:25:42,500
you can share that story

671
00:25:42,500 --> 00:25:44,500
and tell the scouts that it took a lot of work

